{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>the nobles of the people dug it.</b> Duplicated, as is the rule." "<b>with a scepter.</b> By means of lawgivers, like לבי לחוקקי ישראל (my heart is with the lawgivers of Israel). And this well was in the wilderness, far from settlement. From this wilderness they journeyed to Mattanah, and from there to Nahaliel. Know that Ashd-ha-Nahalim and the wilderness called Be'er and Mattanah and Nahaliel are all places, and they have a general name, which is Almon-diblathaim, for so it is written in the section אלה מסעי, or these are names of places that they passed over in a later journey. And behold, the Avarim opposite Nevo — it is the Bamot and the valley that is in the field of Moab. And the proof is that Scripture says that from the valley they journeyed to the plains of Moab, across from Jericho's Jordan, and it is written that from Mount Ha-Avarim they journeyed to the plains of Moab, by Jericho's Jordan. And further: ונשב בגיא מול בית פעור (and we sat in the valley opposite Beth-Peor) — the time when I entreated. And in another place: עלה אל הר העברים הר נבו (go up to Mount Ha-Avarim, Mount Nevo); and also ויקבוד אותו בגיא (and he buried him in the valley), and there it is written: ויעל משה מערבות מואב אל הר נבו (and Moses went up from the plains of Moab to Mount Nevo). And so the valley is the top of the summit, and there Moses died, and there is no need to transport him after his death."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra quotes Deuteronomy 3:29 as ונשב בגיא מול בית פעור; the received text reads ונשבתי. He may be citing from memory or following a variant tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:45.811790818Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}